# Frontend routing

Apply the target app's `AGENTS.md` first:

- Admin index: `admin-panel/docs/README.md`
- Client index: `client/docs/README.md`
- Shared cross-app rules: `docs/frontend/README.md`

## Shared boundaries

- Next.js 16.3, React 19, App Router, Tailwind CSS v4, Persian RTL-first.
- Read the target app's installed `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before
  version-sensitive Next.js work; installed docs override model memory.
- Prefer Server Components and small client boundaries. Use `proxy.ts`, not new
  `middleware.ts`, for request interception.
- The API base already includes `/api/v1`; never prefix helper paths with `/v1/`.
- NestJS owns persistence, auth, business rules, and agents.
- Positive-only JSX uses `{condition && <Component />}` with strings/numbers
  coerced first; ternaries require two meaningful UI branches.

## High-frequency app rules

- Admin Base UI Select/menu/overlay work must load
  `admin-panel/docs/development/components.md`: visible Select label children,
  `alignItemWithTrigger={false}`, grouped menu labels, and task-based overlay
  choice.
- Client dashboard layout work must load
  `client/docs/engineering/ui.md#customer-dashboard-loading-skeletons`: keep a
  co-located, structure-matched loading skeleton in the same change.

Detailed examples remain in those app-local documents; do not copy generic
Radix examples into the Base UI admin app.
